Ein's patch to lrpar 0.15.0 (M1f S1f.5.5, F11; T1f.5.5.3, 2026-11-08).

This directory is the crate as published on crates.io (git 0fd68c80cb13, its
.cargo_vcs_info.json), with grmtools' COPYRIGHT, LICENSE-APACHE and LICENSE-MIT
at that commit, which the published crate does not carry, and this diff. To
re-apply it to a fresh copy: `patch -p1 < ein.patch` from the crate's root.

- The ranking: duplicate repair sequences are dropped keeping the first of
  each, in the order the search found them, and the sort is stable, so equal
  repairs keep the search's order. Upstream de-duplicated through a HashSet
  and sorted unstably, so one input could report its repairs in two orders.
- The budget: recovery is bounded by RECOVERY_STEP_BUDGET search steps over the
  whole parse, not by 500 ms of wall clock, so an input reports the same
  errors on every machine and under any load.
- The cut: each ParseError says how many steps recovery had taken
  (recovery_steps) and whether the budget stopped it there (recovery_cut), so
  that an error with no repairs because recovery ran out reads differently
  from one with none at all.

